# Device safety (AAOS / adb)

When changing anything on a connected Android Automotive device:

## Forbidden

- `adb reboot recovery`, `adb reboot bootloader`, `adb reboot fastboot`, `adb reboot sideload`
- `fastboot` flash/erase/format/unlock commands
- `adb wipe`, factory reset, `recovery --wipe_*`
- Deleting stock overlay backups (`*.orig`, `*.stock-bak`)
- Pushing **unsigned** or signature-broken APKs to `/system*` or `/system_ext/overlay`
- Disabling verity / AVB beyond what `adb remount` already requires on a userdebug build

## Required

- Confirm `adb devices` shows `device` (not `recovery` / `sideload` / `bootloader`) before changes
- Prefer `scripts/lib/device-safety.sh` / `.ps1` helpers for remount overlay installs
- Backup remote overlay before replace; keep `/system_ext/overlay/DewdDynamicAospRRO.apk.orig`
- After reboot: wait for `sys.boot_completed=1`; if boot fails or mode ≠ Android, restore stock overlay and `adb reboot` (normal only)
- On Dewd (`car.dewd.config=dynamic`): use `install-prebuilts.* -Dewd` / `--dewd` only — never enable Design SystemUI RRO alone

## Allowed reboots

Only: `adb reboot` (normal Android boot).
